From c80c188f4ee869b50569f12e4fec60ff0dd8127c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:19:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] test(post): pin the G76 readings that two published manuals
 settle

Three of the four open G76 readings of the Fanuc lathe post agree with
the FANUC 0i-F lathe operator's manual (B-64604EN-1, 4.2.7) and the
Siemens SINUMERIK ISO Turning manual (A5E52211627B, G76): the start
point and the flank shift along the travel, every pass ending at the
programmed end point, and the minimum depth clamping the cut of one
pass. New tests pin each one; the shared fixture moves to
tests/common/g76.rs (the schedule suite stood at the 400-line law).
The internal rounding of dd*sqrt(n) stays open. No posted G-code
changes. Follow-up for the pass-end difference: #1896.

Refs #1842

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
